description:
Commit 8d8b6c5 added four new params structs to src/methods/mod.rs:

- MetadataGetParams (line 38)
- MetadataSetParams (line 60)
- MetadataQueryParams (line 127)
- MetadataQueryChangesParams (line 148)

All four are #[derive(Debug, Default, serde::Serialize)] — no Clone. They join the pre-existing MetadataChangesParams (line 87) flagged at wzq9.20, which is BLOCKED at P3 pending the canonical-template propagation decision.

Why this is filed separately from wzq9.20 — wzq9.20 was filed against the pre-feat-commit state (only MetadataChangesParams existed). The four new structs were introduced AFTER wzq9.20's description was written; they inherit the same gap by being cookie-cut from canonical mail-client (whose EmailGetParams, EmailCopyParams, MailboxSetParams, EmailSubmissionSetParams, EmailParseParams are all also Serialize-only without Clone — see crate-jmap-mail-client/src/methods/mod.rs:40,67,87,111,253). This finding confirms that wzq9.20's propagation note now covers a 5-struct surface in metadata-client (one of which was its original target).

Engineering rationale (extending wzq9.20's pagination argument): a caller running multiple Metadata/* calls with the same vendor extras cannot reuse the params struct because the methods take 'params: Option<MetadataXxxParams>' by value (metadata.rs:55, :203, :288, :327). With Clone, the idiomatic pattern is:

    let mut p = MetadataQueryParams::default();
    p.extra.insert("acmeCorpAnchor".into(), json!(cursor));
    loop {
        let resp = sc.metadata_query(filter.clone(), sort.clone(), Some(pos), Some(50), Some(p.clone())).await?;
        if resp.ids.is_empty() { break; }
        pos += 50;
    }

Without Clone the caller must reconstruct the params (rebuild the extras Map) on every iteration. This is a real ergonomic gap, not just for pagination — anywhere multiple calls share the same extras.

Fix: add Clone to all five params struct derives. Cost is bounded by the extras Map size (per wzq9.5's documented allocation budget: typically zero or single-digit keys); no semantic risk on Serialize-only types.

Propagation footprint (per wzq9.20's note and the workspace canonical-template rule): this is one fix that must land on canonical mail-client's five params structs first, then propagate to all seven extension-client siblings (jmap-chat-client, jmap-calendars-client, jmap-tasks-client, jmap-contacts-client, jmap-filenode-client, jmap-metadata-client, jmap-sharing-client) — wherever they exist or are added. Filing under wzq9 only; the wider propagation is the canonical-mail-client maintainer's call.

Relationship to wzq9.20: wzq9.20 remains the parent decision-bead. This finding is a scope-confirmation, not a competing finding. If wzq9.20 closes with 'add Clone to all five metadata-client params types', this finding closes with it.
